e. realize a social life that is safe and free from all forms of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women.

CHAPTER IX
OBLIGATIONS OF THE CITY REGIONAL GOVERNMENT
Article 30
(1) The obligations of the City Regional Government in the implementation of Women's Protection are as follows:
a. formulate policies and incorporate Women's Protection programs in regional development planning and budgeting;
b. provide complaint services, health services, social rehabilitation, assistance and law enforcement as well as repatriation and social reintegration for women victims;
c. establish shelter services and/or safe houses;
d. establish special mechanisms for integrated hospital-based services;
e. establish PPT;
f. establish the UPT for Women and Children Protection;
g. formulate standard operating procedures and service referral systems;
h. conduct prevention of violence, exploitation and discrimination against women;
i. provide human resources and infrastructure facilities for Women's Protection;
j. increase support and develop women's protection service institutions owned by the City Regional Government and the community;
k. develop victim services based on communities, boarding educational institutions, basic educational institutions, religious institutions, and the business sector;
l. conduct capacity building;
m. conduct coordination and cooperation;
n. conduct empowerment to increase community participation;
o. develop an integrated and interconnected data and information system for women's protection;
p. conduct control, guidance and supervision of the implementation of women's protection services; and
q. provide awards to the community, community organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, boarding educational institutions, the business sector and other parties.
(2) Planning and budgeting for Women's Protection as referred to in paragraph (1) letter a shall be the responsibility of the Regional Apparatus implementing supporting functions of Government Affairs and the Service (Dinas).

CHAPTER II
WOMEN'S RIGHTS
Article 5
Every Woman has the right to:
a. obtain information related to the Protection of Women, victim service procedures and developments in case handling;
b. report, provide statements and views without pressure;
c. participate in case handling and in efforts to eliminate violence against women;
d. obtain protection of confidentiality;
e. obtain protection for personal security, family and property from threats and violence;
f. be free from all forms of stereotypes, stigma and other discrimination;
g. obtain services and recovery needed;
h. obtain restitution; and
i. form and join organizations.

Article 17
(1) Reproductive health services as referred to in Article 12 paragraph (1) letter c, constitute a state of complete physical, mental, and social well-being related to the system, functions, and processes of reproduction, not merely the absence of disease or disability.
(2) Reproductive health services are implemented through activities in the form of:
a. early detection of disease or screening;
b. treatment;
c. rehabilitation;
d. counseling; and
e. provision of contraceptive devices.

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD,
THE MAYOR OF CIREBON,
Considering : a. that every woman has the right to obtain a sense of security and protection from all forms of violence, exploitation, torture, discrimination, and other mistreatment that degrades human dignity and violates human rights;
b. that to ensure the prevention and handling of acts of violence against women in a fast, accurate, comprehensive, and integrated manner, regulation regarding the protection of women is required;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women from Violence, Exploitation and Discrimination;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95);
3. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning the Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635), as amended by Law Number 31 of 2014 concerning the Amendment to Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning the Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 293, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5602);
4. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
5. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587), as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 6 of 2023 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);
6. Law Number 30 of 2014 concerning Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 292, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5601), as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 6 of 2023 concerning the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);
7. Law Number 12 of 2022 concerning the Criminal Act of Sexual Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2022 Number 120, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6792);
8. Law Number 17 of 2023 concerning Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2023 Number 105, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6887);
9. Law Number 108 of 2024 concerning the City of Cirebon in the Province of West Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2024 Number 294, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 7045);
10. Government Regulation Number 28 of 2024 concerning the Implementing Regulation of Law Number 17 of 2023 concerning Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2024 Number 135, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6952);
11. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 4 of 2023 concerning Acting Governor, Acting Regent, and Acting Mayor (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2023 Number 310);
12. Decree of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 100.2.1.3-6572 of 2023 concerning the Appointment of the Acting Mayor of Cirebon, Province of West Java;
13. Regional Regulation of the City of Cirebon Number 9 of 2016 concerning the Formation of Regional Legal Products (Regional Gazette of the City of Cirebon Year 2016 Number 9), as amended by Regional Regulation of the City of Cirebon Number 5 of 2020 concerning the Amendment to Regional Regulation Number 9 of 2016 concerning the Formation of Regional Legal Products (Regional Gazette of the City of Cirebon Year 2020 Number 5);
